{
  "summary": "Reported: Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5) asks whether a rumored \"verify your payroll login\" email is legitimate. She says she heard about it going around; she did not report clicking or entering anything. Checked: account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked. Her quarantine has message Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain: capital I in place of lowercase l in 'brightline'), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login\", received 2026-10-09 09:03 UTC, marked phishing and not releasable. It was caught in quarantine, so it likely never reached her inbox. She says it is \"going around\", so other users have probably received it too. Needed: security review of the sender and lookalike domain, an org-wide block, and a check for copies that got past the filter into other users' inboxes. Not released (phishing). No compromise indicators for this user.",
  "reason": "KB-008: reported phishing email must always be escalated for sender review/blocking; likely multiple recipients"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for checking before acting on it. Reports like yours help the security team find new scams. That email is not real. It's a phishing scam. We found a copy that was sent to you on the morning of Oct 9. It looked like it came from 'IT support', but the sender's address only looks like ours: it has a capital I where the lowercase l in 'brightline' should be. Our filter caught it and held it back, so it shouldn't have reached your inbox. We will never ask you to verify your payroll login by email, and your payroll isn't affected. If you or anyone else sees it, please don't click, reply, or forward it. Leave it where it is so security can look at it. I've sent this to our security team so they can review the sender and block it for everyone. One question: did you click a link in an email like this or type your password anywhere? If you did, reply right away or call the help desk so we can secure your account.",
  "internal_note": "The user asked whether a rumored payroll-verification email is real. Her account is active with 0 failed logins and is not blocked. Her quarantine holds Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain), subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-09 09:03 UTC. It is marked phishing, not releasable, and was not released. She did not report any interaction, so there was no reason to run the KB-029 steps. I asked her to confirm she didn't click or enter credentials. Escalated to Tier 2 under KB-008 (escalation 1) for sender review and an org-wide block. She says it is going around, so it likely hit several users.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
